Great question. Right now, **the `Delete` key press is not handled for deleting nodes from the tree view**.

If you want to support deleting nodes using the `Delete` key, you can wire up a `KeyDown` event for the `RadTreeView` and implement logic similar to this:

### ✅ Add this in `WireEvents()`:
```csharp
radTreeView_TarrifRateTables.KeyDown += RadTreeView_TarrifRateTables_KeyDown;
```

### ✅ And then implement the handler:
```csharp
private async void RadTreeView_TarrifRateTables_KeyDown(object sender, KeyEventArgs e)
{
    if (e.KeyCode == Keys.Delete && radTreeView_TarrifRateTables.SelectedNode?.Tag is TreeViewNodeModel model)
    {
        var confirm = MessageBox.Show($"Delete this {model.modelType}?", "Confirm Delete", MessageBoxButtons.YesNo, MessageBoxIcon.Warning);
        if (confirm == DialogResult.Yes)
        {
            await DeleteNodeAsync(model);
        }
    }
}
```

This will catch the `Delete` key on the selected node and safely call your existing delete logic, including confirmation.

